The entire screen is no longer cleared for every frame. Each buffer keeps track of the last frame it contains (`buffer_frames[0]` or `[1]`), as the two buffers alternate, with each one lagging one frame behind what is currently visible. To draw the new frame, the system calculates two rectangles: the bar’s previous position—within that same buffer—and its current position. If these rectangles overlap, they are merged; if the bar jumps from one edge to the other, they remain separate. The background, the bar, and any static rectangles are then redrawn only within those specific areas.
